WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:01.695
(driving orchestral music)

00:00:01.695 --> 00:00:02.528
- [Narrator] At New York's

00:00:02.528 --> 00:00:04.335
American Museum of Natural History,

00:00:04.335 --> 00:00:05.867
we are past the Roosevelt Atrium,

00:00:05.867 --> 00:00:06.924
through the Frick Building,

00:00:06.924 --> 00:00:08.874
and tucked away behind drawers of bones,

00:00:08.874 --> 00:00:11.023
Doctor Jack Tseng is hard at work.

00:00:11.023 --> 00:00:12.381
He's a dog guy.

00:00:12.381 --> 00:00:14.405
- Well, I have worked on dog evolution

00:00:14.405 --> 00:00:17.208
and dog fossil for about 10 years.

00:00:17.208 --> 00:00:19.727
- [Narrator] Jack's the man
when it comes to dog evolution,

00:00:19.727 --> 00:00:23.894
and he says dogs might have
a shot at outliving us all.

00:00:26.105 --> 00:00:28.267
(moves into light orchestral music)

00:00:28.267 --> 00:00:29.360
- [Narrator] Humans have been evolving

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.727
for roughly 3 million years,

00:00:31.727 --> 00:00:34.045
but dogs have been around way longer.

00:00:34.045 --> 00:00:37.340
- And that history goes all
the way back 40 million years.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:38.435
- [Narrator] It hasn't been easy.

00:00:38.435 --> 00:00:39.268
(chirping)

00:00:39.268 --> 00:00:41.773
They've dealt with warming,
cooling, the Ice Age.

00:00:41.773 --> 00:00:43.627
To determine how dogs are going to fare

00:00:43.627 --> 00:00:44.760
as the world changes,
(digital whizzing)

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.510
you have to start in the past.

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:49.199
Because dogs are evolutionary marvels.

00:00:49.199 --> 00:00:51.958
The first dogs weren't really
dogs as we know them today.

00:00:51.958 --> 00:00:54.159
They were tree-dwellers and really small.

00:00:54.159 --> 00:00:55.850
They changed to survive.
(whooshing)

00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:57.043
They're legs lengthened
(digital beeping)

00:00:57.043 --> 00:00:57.876
so they could run
(whooshing)

00:00:57.876 --> 00:01:00.675
longer distances and they grew a lot.

00:01:00.675 --> 00:01:01.748
During the Ice Age,
(whooshing)

00:01:01.748 --> 00:01:04.983
the big wolves weighed around 140 pounds.

00:01:04.983 --> 00:01:06.136
But it's their teeth

00:01:06.136 --> 00:01:08.588
that are really the key to their survival.

00:01:08.588 --> 00:01:10.107
- Their teeth were getting stronger

00:01:10.107 --> 00:01:11.348
to deal with a larger bones

00:01:11.348 --> 00:01:12.293
and the grit
(whooshing)

00:01:12.293 --> 00:01:13.126
that they make
(clicking)

00:01:13.126 --> 00:01:15.146
in your mouth when you're hunting.

00:01:15.146 --> 00:01:17.080
- [Narrator] What he's saying
is that it's biological

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:19.925
that dogs are eating machines.

00:01:19.925 --> 00:01:20.770
Think of their teeth
(whooshing)

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:21.894
as a basic blueprint
(digital beeping)

00:01:21.894 --> 00:01:24.132
that goes back 40 million years

00:01:24.132 --> 00:01:26.036
and can be adapted to any kind

00:01:26.036 --> 00:01:27.693
of environmental change.
(digital beep)

00:01:27.693 --> 00:01:29.301
The teeth in the back crush bone,

00:01:29.301 --> 00:01:30.134
those teeth
(digital beep)

00:01:30.134 --> 00:01:31.252
in the middle are for cutting,

00:01:31.252 --> 00:01:32.139
and the front teeth
(digital beep)

00:01:32.139 --> 00:01:33.253
are for puncturing.

00:01:33.253 --> 00:01:34.219
What's more,
(whooshing)

00:01:34.219 --> 00:01:36.655
dogs teeth have reinforced surfaces.

00:01:36.655 --> 00:01:37.749
That means their teeth
(crunching)

00:01:37.749 --> 00:01:39.616
will stay in tact whether they're eating

00:01:39.616 --> 00:01:40.449
large bones
(whooshing)

00:01:40.449 --> 00:01:42.449
or chewing up carcasses.

00:01:43.786 --> 00:01:46.391
It also means dogs don't really need us.

00:01:46.391 --> 00:01:47.224
(light dreamy music)

00:01:47.224 --> 00:01:49.378
They'll be able to survive
even if we're no longer around

00:01:49.378 --> 00:01:51.119
to feed them, because they can eat

00:01:51.119 --> 00:01:53.975
pretty much anything that comes their way.

00:01:53.975 --> 00:01:56.919
- If we do go and they're
alive, I'm sure they will adapt

00:01:56.919 --> 00:02:00.669
to whatever environment
that comes their way.

